      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "answer": "Current law does not address religious displays in public school classrooms. The measure changes this by legally requiring every public school classroom to display a poster of the Ten Commandments.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "answer": "Direct costs include the production, distribution, and installation of the posters for every public school classroom. There may also be significant legal costs if the mandate is challenged in court.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "answer": "Unless private donations cover the acquisition of the posters, public school districts and taxpayers will bear the cost of purchasing and displaying them, as well as the cost of any resulting litigation.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "answer": "Schools will need to procure the posters to comply with the mandate. Advocacy groups are likely to initiate legal challenges regarding the separation of church and state.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "answer": "The text does not state the problem it seeks to address. The mechanism mandates the presence of a specific religious text in the learning environment of public schools.",
      "disputed": false
    }
  ],
